[AS7's Example 12.12 (unbalanced delta-delta)]

e0a,0,ag,(208∠130°)
eb0,bg,0,(208∠-110°)
rla,ag,ad,2+5j
rlb,bg,bd,2+5j
rlc,0,cd,2+5j
rab,ad,bd,50
rbc,bd,cd,30j
rca,cd,ad,-40j

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: The generator current Iab cannot be had this way: it is a current inside the delta, and the two-source trick gives up exactly that.
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


[AS7's Example 12.5 (balanced delta-wye)]

eca,c,a,(210∠120°)
ebc,b,c,(210∠-120°)
ra,a,0,40+25j
rb,b,0,40+25j
rc,c,0,40+25j

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: Node 0 here is the centre of the load's wye, not a node of the source at all.
